---
description: Global project architecture and file-size rules
globs: "**/*.{ts,tsx,js,jsx}"
alwaysApply: true
---

# Core Rules

- Keep every file under 300 lines.
- If a file reaches 250 lines, split it immediately.
- Prefer Next.js Server Components by default.
- Add `"use client"` only when required by hooks/browser APIs.

# Modular Structure

- Move complex UI logic into `@/hooks`.
- Move API and integration logic into `@/services`.
- Move shared app state into `@/lib/store`.
- Move shared domain types into `@/types`.

# AI App Focus

- Keep AI orchestration centralized in reusable store/hooks.
- Avoid duplicating AI logic across pages.
- Mount global AI entry points in `app/layout.tsx`.

# PR-ready (before merge)

- Run `npm run lint`. If types touched: `npx tsc --noEmit`.
- Note risks (auth, RLS, secrets, edge deploy). DB change: add rollback note.
- Never paste or commit secrets. Client only `NEXT_PUBLIC_*`.

# Cursor helpers

- Project detail: `.cursor/rules/project-rules.mdc`, `.cursor/rules/agent-automation.mdc`.
- Agents: `.cursor/agents/project-shipper.md`, `project-reviewer.md`.
- Commands: `.cursor/commands/ship.md`, `fix.md`, `review.md`, `test.md`.
